"considered as part of later proposals, but they will be handled in a more "
"incremental fashion, rather than as a single large proposed change with no "
"feasible migration plan."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0426.rst:35
msgid "Abstract"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0426.rst:37
msgid ""
"This PEP describes a mechanism for publishing and exchanging metadata "
"related to Python distributions. It includes specifics of the field names, "
"and their semantics and usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0426.rst:41
msgid ""
"This document specifies the never released version 2.0 of the metadata "
"format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0426.rst:43
msgid ""
"Version 1.0 is specified in :pep:`241`. Version 1.1 is specified in :pep:"
"`314`. Version 1.2 is specified in :pep:`345`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0426.rst:47
msgid ""
"Version 2.0 of the metadata format proposed migrating from directly defining "
"a custom key-value file format to instead defining a JSON-compatible in-"
"memory representation that may be used to define metadata representation in "
"other contexts (such as API and archive format definitions)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0426.rst:52
msgid ""
"This version also defines a formal extension mechanism, allowing new fields "
"to be added for particular purposes without requiring updates to the core "
"metadata format."
msgstr ""

